  "rule": "The background is 1, and the colour-4 figure is the template. Every other colour shows a partial, translated-only copy of that template. Complete each fragment into a full template copy in its own colour, using the shift that covers the most fragment cells while landing only on background or the same colour inside the grid. Repeat this per colour until every fragment cell is covered. Never erase cells.",
  "scope": "Supported: random 8-connected templates of 5..8 cells in boxes of up to 5x5. Random grids are 14..30 per side, including non-square sizes; grids larger than the fixtures are synthetic extensions. Scenes have 1..7 fragment colours from {2,3,5,6,7,8,9}, each fragment 2..4 cells. Optionally one colour owns two fragments. Some copies are placed against a border so the grid bounds help disambiguate. Callers may pass an explicit template shape, template position and full explicit copies for fixture reconstruction. Not supported: rotated or mirrored copies, overlapping or touching objects, a template colour other than 4, a background other than 1, fragments that already show the whole template, and more than two fragments per colour in random mode.",
  "constraints": [
    "1100 independent input-only exhaustive placement checks; all original fixtures exact",
    "All maximal-coverage tie branches produce the same completed grid; 295 multi-copy-colour cases and 2490 border-completed colours",
    "22 successful parameter controls and eight invalid-control rejections; 100 explicit 30x30 seven-colour cases"
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
    "Background 1 and template colour 4 are fixed, as in all original examples.",
    "Template shapes are limited to 5..8 cells within a 5x5 box in random mode.",
    "The ambiguity filter mirrors the greedy max-coverage semantics of the verified explanation. It checks rule-consistency of the intended answer locally and does not consult the archived solver.",
    "Small explicit grids combined with many colours, or highly symmetric user-supplied shapes, may exhaust retries and raise RuntimeError.",
    "Random generation is biased toward larger grids when many colours are requested, because placement in small grids fails more often.",
    "Bounded validation is not proof of complete task semantics."
  ],
