  "authored_scope": "Supported: random 8-connected templates of 5..8 cells in boxes of up to 5x5. Random grids are 14..30 per side, including non-square sizes; grids larger than the fixtures are synthetic extensions. Scenes have 1..7 fragment colours from {2,3,5,6,7,8,9}, each fragment 2..4 cells. Optionally one colour owns two fragments. Some copies are placed against a border so the grid bounds help disambiguate. Callers may pass an explicit template shape, template position and full explicit copies for fixture reconstruction. Not supported: rotated or mirrored copies, overlapping or touching objects, a template colour other than 4, a background other than 1, fragments that already show the whole template, and more than two fragments per colour in random mode.",
  "authored_constraints": [
    "Object bounding boxes (template and every copy) are separated by at least one background row or column, so copies never collide or touch.",
    "count(1) > count(4) > count(any fragment colour), so both the background and the template colour are identified by frequency.",
    "Each colour's total fragment cells are fewer than the template's cell count, so every sample is non-identity.",
    "A simulated greedy max-coverage completion must recover exactly the intended copies for each colour. Ties are allowed only among intended copies, and no rule-consistent alternative shift may tie or win.",
    "In random scenes the four input corner cells are background.",
    "The template shape is normalised, 8-connected and two-dimensional.",
    "Explicit scenes are validated with the same checks (except the corner rule) and raise ValueError when invalid.",
    "All retry loops are bounded (at most 300 scene attempts x 30 fragment draws). Exhaustion raises RuntimeError."
  ],
